WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.588
The next morning, Heidi opened her eyes.

2
00:00:02.589 --> 00:00:06.656
She was in a high bed facing two windows covered by long curtains.

3
00:00:06.657 --> 00:00:12.970
It was very different from her bed in the hayloft, with its view down the valley through the hole by her bed.

4
00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:15.831
Heidi jumped out of bed and ran to a window.

5
00:00:15.832 --> 00:00:20.241
The curtains were too heavy for her to push aside, so she crawled under them.

6
00:00:20.242 --> 00:00:23.099
Behind the curtains, the window was too high.

7
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.618
She could only just peer out and couldn’t find a way to open it.

8
00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:29.063
Suddenly there was a knock on her door.

9
00:00:29.064 --> 00:00:31.783
"Breakfast is ready," said the maid.

10
00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:35.785
Heidi had no idea what she was expected to do, so she waited.

11
00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:38.119
Shortly after, Fraulein appeared.

12
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.048
"What is the matter with you, Heidi?" she said angrily."Don’t

13
00:00:42.049 --> 00:00:44.939
you understand what breakfast is? Come

14
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.062
along at once!" Heidi

15
00:00:47.063 --> 00:00:49.745
had no difficulty understanding that. She

16
00:00:49.746 --> 00:00:52.136
followed Fraulein downstairs. The

17
00:00:52.137 --> 00:00:56.015
windows in the dining room were also too high for her to see out of.

18
00:00:56.016 --> 00:00:59.276
Heidi was starting to feel like she was in a prison.

19
00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:03.478
Clara had been at the breakfast table for a while and was smiling cheerfully.

20
00:01:03.479 --> 00:01:07.179
Heidi didn’t know it, but Clara was often lonely and glum.

21
00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:13.714
Now that Heidi was staying with her, Clara was looking forward to all sorts of new fun.

22
00:01:13.715 --> 00:01:16.887
As soon as the children were alone, Heidi asked,

23
00:01:16.888 --> 00:01:19.935
"How can I open a window in my bedroom?"

24
00:01:19.936 --> 00:01:21.673
"You can ask Sebastian.

25
00:01:21.674 --> 00:01:25.107
He’ll be happy to open one for you," Clara assured her.

26
00:01:25.108 --> 00:01:27.291
Heidi was very relieved.

27
00:01:27.292 --> 00:01:30.712
While the girls were eating breakfast, Clara’s tutor arrived.

28
00:01:30.713 --> 00:01:34.477
Fraulein took him aside and told him all her worries about Heidi.

29
00:01:34.478 --> 00:01:39.575
He was a patient man and said that regular teaching would soon help her catch up to Clara.

30
00:01:39.576 --> 00:01:44.426
After breakfast, the girls joined him in the study and started their lesson.

31
00:01:44.427 --> 00:01:49.825
A little while later, Fraulein was walking past the study door when she heard a huge crash.

32
00:01:49.826 --> 00:01:52.182
"Look at the state of things!"

33
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:54.702
exclaimed Fraulein when she opened the door.

34
00:01:54.703 --> 00:01:59.715
"Tablecloth, books, work basket, everything covered in ink.

35
00:01:59.716 --> 00:02:03.973
It was Heidi’s fault, I suppose!"

36
00:02:03.974 --> 00:02:07.742
"Yes, but it was all an accident," said Clara.

37
00:02:07.743 --> 00:02:11.867
"Heidi heard the carriages passing outside, and they startled her."Fraulein

38
00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:15.184
was angry, but did not punish Heidi. Later

39
00:02:15.185 --> 00:02:22.442
that afternoon, while Clara took her nap, Heidi asked Sebastian where she could go to see out over the whole city. "You

40
00:02:22.443 --> 00:02:27.202
would have to climb to the top of a church tower," said Sebastian. With

41
00:02:27.203 --> 00:02:31.764
that in mind, Heidi set off in search of the highest tower she could find. On

42
00:02:31.765 --> 00:02:35.450
a street corner, she saw a boy with a hand organ and asked, "Do

43
00:02:35.451 --> 00:02:38.789
you know any churches with high towers?"

44
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.647
"Yes, I know one.

45
00:02:40.648 --> 00:02:44.357
For two pennies, I will show you," the boy said.

46
00:02:44.358 --> 00:02:45.786
"Clara will pay you.

47
00:02:45.787 --> 00:02:48.112
She has money," Heidi agreed.

48
00:02:48.113 --> 00:02:51.600
"And will you help me find my way back home?" she asked.

49
00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:54.052
"Yes, for another two pennies."

50
00:02:54.053 --> 00:02:56.540
"Okay," said Heidi.

51
00:02:56.541 --> 00:02:59.384
The boy led her through the streets to an old church.

52
00:02:59.385 --> 00:03:05.022
A priest answered the bell and, holding her hand, led Heidi up the winding stairs.

53
00:03:05.023 --> 00:03:08.603
At the top, Heidi was disappointed.

54
00:03:08.604 --> 00:03:11.103
"I wanted to see the mountains.

55
00:03:11.104 --> 00:03:16.590
All I can see are roofs and towers and chimney tops!" she said.

56
00:03:16.591 --> 00:03:20.162
"I have something else to show you," said the priest.

57
00:03:20.163 --> 00:03:21.334
"Follow me."

58
00:03:21.335 --> 00:03:25.946
At the bottom of the stairs, behind a closet door, he showed her a basket.

59
00:03:25.947 --> 00:03:28.307
Heidi bent down and said with delight,

60
00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:31.498
"Oh, look at the sweet little kittens!"

61
00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:34.178
"Would you like to have them?" asked the priest.

62
00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:38.227
Heidi could hardly contain her joy.

